##############################################
# CODE EXPLANATION: MW–M31 Halo Shape Pipeline
##############################################

Purpose:
--------
Process MW & M31 dark matter snapshots to quantify halo shape evolution.
Compute metrics for both traditional (inertia tensor) and geometric (convex hull) approaches.

Modules & Functions:
-------------------

1. compute_inertia_tensor(positions, masses)
   - Vectorized computation of mass-weighted inertia tensor
   - Complexity: O(N), Memory: O(1) extra
   - Input: particle positions relative to COM, masses
   - Output: 3x3 inertia tensor

2. inertia_axis_ratios(I)
   - Eigenvalues → b/a, c/a
   - Returns eigenvalues for ellipsoidal volume calculation

3. ellipsoid_volume_from_inertia(eigvals)
   - Compute equivalent ellipsoid volume: V = 4/3 π a b c

4. convex_hull_properties(positions)
   - Compute convex hull of particles
   - Axis ratios from covariance of hull vertices
   - Complexity: O(M log M), M = #hull vertices

5. triaxiality(b_over_a, c_over_a)
   - Compute T = (1-(b/a)^2)/(1-(c/a)^2)
   - Interpret halo as oblate/prolate/triaxial

6. sphericity(c_over_a)
   - S = c/a

7. load_and_center_snapshots(mw_file, m31_file, centering)
   - Concatenate MW & M31 particles
   - Center using MW COM or barycenter
   - Output: positions, masses, centering coordinates

8. process_snapshots(snapshot_range, data_dir, centering, output_file)
   - Loops over snapshots:
       • Loads & centers particles
       • Computes inertia & convex hull metrics
       • Computes derived quantities: triaxiality, sphericity, volume inflation
       • Logs optional print statements
   - Saves all metrics to HDF5 for reproducibility
   - Optimizations:
       • Preallocated arrays → O(n_snapshots) memory
       • Vectorized tensor → O(N) per snapshot
       • Hull uses only vertices → memory & time efficient

